  attachedPhoto: {fileID: 0}
  logText: 'We have finally made our first jump, leaving our home behind. As expected,
    most of us woke up feeling quite dizzy, and it took a couple of hours to fully
    recover. Marcus continues to dwell on the long term effects that faster-than-light
    travel could have on us, but there''s no point in worrying now. We have a mission
    to carry out, and all of humanity depends on us now.


    One month from now,
    team 1 will be detaching from the main ship and setting out to explore the first
    solar system. Small probes have made it this far, back when FTL was being tested,
    but it will be the first time a person touches a planet outside our own solar
    system. As part of team 10, it will be a long while before I get to do some exploration
    myself, but there''s plenty of work to do in the meantime.


    And... so many
    jumps left. Can''t say I''m looking forward to that.'
  orderFound: 0
  read: 1
